KG42.register("rules-af8835267c859d7581c01a5b",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R002","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R002","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Supply submission","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The coordinator limits supply-bid updates by evenly randomly selecting a predefined-size set of participants forbidden to change their energy bids at each iteration. Scope: Optional bid-count step length control in iterative P2P energy bidding; selection covers all participants and applies to supply bids among their submissions. Condition: Bid-count control is adopted; the supply bid belongs to a participant selected into the forbidden set. The coordinator must reject a supply bid whose change exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit. Scope: Proposed practical coordinator enforcement of optional bid-ramping control in P2P energy bidding. Condition: The proposed enforcement rule is adopted and a supply bid exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit. SDR supply bids follow the energy-bid content specification in Formula (A18), derived from the participant's decision-making-model results. Scope: Supply quantities represented within SDR energy bids during the iterative bidding process. Condition: The energy bid is negative at the relevant time step. Supply-bid changes at each iteration must respect the prescribed ramping allowance around the previous bid, with the resulting bounds clipped to the minimum and maximum energy-bid limits. Scope: Supply energy-bid constraints in the simulation's iterative decision-making model. Condition: The bid-ramping form of optional step length control is adopted. The two controls may be combined by first limiting the number of bids allowed to change and then limiting changes to the allowable supply bids. Scope: Supply-bid updates under optional combined step length control. Condition: Bid-count control and bid-ramping control are used together.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function bidding.supply under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"bidding.supply","type":"limits","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g03-E11"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Optional bid-count step length control in iterative P2P energy bidding; selection covers all participants and applies to supply bids among their submissions. | Proposed practical coordinator enforcement of optional bid-ramping control in P2P energy bidding. | Supply energy-bid constraints in the simulation's iterative decision-making model. | Supply quantities represented within SDR energy bids during the iterative bidding process. | Supply-bid updates under optional combined step length control.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E02","v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05","v141-b-g07-ev-11"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R002-x-01","symbol":"e^{bid}_{i,j}","meaning":"Energy bid of prosumer agent j at iteration i, restricted in this rule to the supply-bid component when the net bid is negative; the source also uses e^{bid}_i when the prosumer index is implicit.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy-bid quantities for each prosumer j in the participant set and each iteration i of the iterative bidding process; the source gives no numeric domain beyond the minimum and maximum energy-bid limits.","unit":null,"indices":["i","j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E02","v141-b-g03-E04"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-th-rmp","symbol":"rmp","meaning":"Ramping rate used in the step-length-control constraint; the source states it takes a non-negative value.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"non-negative scalar; no universal numeric value is given in this rule"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E02"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-th-emin","symbol":"e^{min}","meaning":"Minimum limit of the energy bid, used as the lower clipping bound in the ramping-rate constraint.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"minimum energy-bid limit; no numeric value is given in this rule"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-th-emax","symbol":"e^{max}","meaning":"Maximum limit of the energy bid, used as the upper clipping bound in the ramping-rate constraint.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"maximum energy-bid limit; no numeric value is given in this rule"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E02"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-th-forbid","symbol":"𝓟𝓐^{forbid}","meaning":"Set of prosumer agents forbidden to change their energy bids at the i-th iteration; its elements are evenly randomly selected by the coordinator, and it is a subset of the prosumer-agent set.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"set of prosumer agents; size is pre-defined and membership is randomly selected by the coordinator each iteration"},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g02-e23"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-th-forbid-size","symbol":"|𝓟𝓐^{forbid}|","meaning":"Pre-defined number of prosumer agents forbidden to change their energy bids at each iteration.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"pre-defined integer; no numeric value is given in this rule"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-th-rmp-prime","symbol":"rmp'","meaning":"Broader ramping rate in the combined step-length-control example, indicating that rmp' × 100% of the bids are allowed to change and each permitted change should not exceed ± rmp' × 100%.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"broader ramping-rate parameter; no numeric value is given in this rule"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g02-e24"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The coordinator limits supply-bid updates by evenly randomly selecting a predefined-size set of participants forbidden to change their energy bids at each iteration. Scope: Optional bid-count step length control in iterative P2P energy bidding; selection covers all participants and applies to supply bids among their submissions. Condition: Bid-count control is adopted; the supply bid belongs to a participant selected into the forbidden set.","expression":"e^{bid}_{i,j} = e^{bid}_{i-1,j},   j ∈ 𝓟𝓐^{forbid} ⊂ 𝓟𝓐   (9)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R002-x-01"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R002-th-forbid"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g02-e23"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The coordinator must reject a supply bid whose change exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit. Scope: Proposed practical coordinator enforcement of optional bid-ramping control in P2P energy bidding. Condition: The proposed enforcement rule is adopted and a supply bid exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g02-e31"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"SDR supply bids follow the energy-bid content specification in Formula (A18), derived from the participant's decision-making-model results. Scope: Supply quantities represented within SDR energy bids during the iterative bidding process. Condition: The energy bid is negative at the relevant time step.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05","v141-b-g07-ev-11"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Supply-bid changes at each iteration must respect the prescribed ramping allowance around the previous bid, with the resulting bounds clipped to the minimum and maximum energy-bid limits. Scope: Supply energy-bid constraints in the simulation's iterative decision-making model. Condition: The bid-ramping form of optional step length control is adopted.","expression":"max(e^{bid}_{i-1,j} - Δ, e^{min}) ≤ e^{bid}_{i,j} ≤ min(e^{bid}_{i-1,j} + Δ, e^{max}),   Δ = rmp · |e^{bid}_{i-1,j}|   (8)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R002-x-01"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R002-th-rmp","v141-c-R002-th-emin","v141-c-R002-th-emax"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E02"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The two controls may be combined by first limiting the number of bids allowed to change and then limiting changes to the allowable supply bids. Scope: Supply-bid updates under optional combined step length control. Condition: Bid-count control and bid-ramping control are used together.","expression":"e^{bid}_{i,j} = e^{bid}_{i-1,j} for j ∈ 𝓟𝓐^{forbid}; and for the remaining allowable bids, max(e^{bid}_{i-1,j} - Δ, e^{min}) ≤ e^{bid}_{i,j} ≤ min(e^{bid}_{i-1,j} + Δ, e^{max}) with Δ = rmp · |e^{bid}_{i-1,j}|.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R002-x-01"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R002-th-forbid","v141-c-R002-th-rmp","v141-c-R002-th-emin","v141-c-R002-th-emax","v141-c-R002-th-rmp-prime"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g02-e24"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e22","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.1","anchor_text":"This technique limits the number or ramping rate of the changing 2P energy/price bids to increase th","equation_id":"8","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Taking the energy bidding process in iterative implementation as an example, the step length control can be achieved by requiring each prosumer agent to limit the ramping rate of the bid at each iteration:\n                bid     min        bid             bid       max                     bid      max( e i − 1−Δ,e    ) \\leqslant e i  \\leqslant min( e i − 1 + Δ,e    ) Δ = rmp ·|e i − 1 |       (8) \nwhere i is the index of the current iteration during which the bid decision needs to be made, and rmp represents the ramping rate that takes a non-negative value. Formula (8) can be basically interpreted as follows: the value of the current energy bid, e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_i, should be bounded in a range, [e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i−1}−Δ,e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i−1}+Δ], which is speciﬁed by the ramping rate and the bid of the previous iteration with Δ = rmp ·|e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i−1}|. Besides, if the upper bound speciﬁed in this way exceeds the maximum limit of the energy bid e^{\\max}, it should be reduced to e^{\\max} by having min(e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i−1} + Δ,e^{\\max}). Similar operation applies to the case of the lower bound. Formula (8) should act as an additional constraint in the decision-making model (as described by Formula (3)) of each prosumer agent."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. bid of the previous iteration with Δ = rmp ·|e ibid− 1 |. Besides, if the upper di bo","equation_id":"9","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The step length control can also be achieved by limiting the number of the bids allowed to be changed at each iteration. That is, e_{i,j}^{bid} = e_{i-1,j}^{bid}, j ∈ 𝓟𝓐^{forbid} ⊂ 𝓟𝓐 (9) where j is the index of prosumer agent. 𝓟𝓐^{forbid} is the set of prosumer agents who are forbidden to change their energy bids at the i th iteration. The number of the elements in 𝓟𝓐^{forbid}, i.e. |𝓟𝓐^{forbid}|, is pre-defined. During simulation, Formula (9) should be added to the decision-making model (as described by Formula (3)) of jth prosumer agent to make it function."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E02","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. bid of the previous iteration with Δ = rmp ·|e ibid− 1 |. Besides, if the upper di bo","equation_id":"8","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"bid of the previous iteration with Δ = rmp ·|e_{i-1}^{bid}|. Besides, if the upper bound specified in this way exceeds the maximum limit of the energy bid e^{max}, it should be reduced to e^{max} by having min(e_{i-1}^{bid} + Δ, e^{max}). Similar operation applies to the case of the lower bound. Formula (8) should act as an additional constraint in the decision-making model (as described by Formula (3)) of each prosumer agent."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"in vergence performance. The eﬀects of this measure with diﬀerent por- re tions of prosumers forbidd","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Note that the two types of step length control patterns are able to be used in a combined way to obtain smaller step limits. That is, one can first limit the number of bids allowed to be changed as described in Formula (9), and then limit the change of the allowable bids by using Formula (8). For example, a broader ramping rate, denoted as rmp′, can be defined, indicating that rmp′ × 100% of the bids are allowed to be changed and the change for each bid should not exceed ± rmp′ × 100%."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E04","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"agents who are forbidden to change their energy bids at the i th itera- p tion. The number of the e","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"At each iteration, the elements of 𝓟𝓐^{forbid}, i.e. the prosumers who are forbidden to change their bids, are evenly randomly selected by the coordinator to ensure the fairness among prosumers. The number of prosumers forbidden affects the magnitude of energy and price change in the region at each iteration, thus potentially affecting the convergence performance."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.3","anchor_text":"y g ( vergence obtained in this way may be far from the feasible optimum). ti th 3.3.3. Practical im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The first technique, step length control, limits the ramping rate of the bids in the bidding process. In practice, this can be realised by the coordinator through setting bidding rules in the implementation model, as described in Section 3.2.4, in a P2P energy sharing mechanism. For example, the mechanism can achieve this by requiring that the coordinator should reject any bid that exceeds the prescribed ramping rate so that all the prosumers have to obey the ramping rate limit. Therefore, the step length control technique in simulation is able to suggest better bidding rules in the implementation model in practice."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-04","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.1","anchor_text":"p g y ⎫ ∈ T ⎬⎭ (A18) he decision-making model consisting of Formulas (A1)–(A17). With the energy ell","equation_id":"A18","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In the SDR mechanism, prosumers are required to provide energy bids for the coordinator at every iteration. Specifically, based on the results of the decision-making model presented in Section A.1, the energy bid of a prosumer is given by\n\ne^{bid} = \\left\\{ e_t^{bid} \\mid e_t^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis} \\right) + P_t^{must-run} - P_{PV,t}, t \\in T \\right\\}  (A18)\n\nin which x^* = \\{x_{\\delta,t}^*, x_t^{ch*}, x_t^{dis*}\\}, \\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f, t \\in T are the optimal solution of the decision-making model consisting of Formulas (A1)-(A17)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-05","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.1","anchor_text":"(A22) (A23) il price between the coordinator and the retailer as illustrated in Fig. 2; SDR haring r","equation_id":"A19-A23","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the energy bids from all the prosumers, the coordinator calculates the internal selling price by\n\np_t^{sell} = \\begin{cases} \\frac{r_t^{export} \\cdot r_t^{retail}}{(r_t^{retail} - r_t^{export}) \\cdot SDR_t + r_t^{export}}, & 0 \\le SDR_t \\le 1 \\\\ r_t^{export}, & SDR_t > 1 \\end{cases}  (A19)\n\nand the internal buying price by\n\np_t^{buy} = \\begin{cases} p_t^{sell} \\cdot SDR_t + r_t^{retail}(1 - SDR_t), & 0 \\le SDR_t \\le 1 \\\\ r_t^{export}, & SDR_t > 1 \\end{cases}  (A20)\n\nin which\n\nSDR_t = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^-} |e_{n,t}^{bid}|}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^+} e_{n,t}^{bid}}  (A21)\n\nwhere\n\n\\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^- = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A} \\}  (A22)\n\nand\n\n\\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^+ = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \\ge 0, n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A} \\}.  (A23)\n\nIn Formulas (A19)-(A23), r_t^{export} and r_t^{retail} are the export and retail price between the coordinator and the retailer as illustrated in Fig. 2; SDR represents the supply and demand ratio of the whole P2P energy sharing region. Formulas (A19)-(A23) establish the pricing model in the coordinator agent under the SDR mechanism."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-11","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p27-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":27,"printed_page":"1019","section":"A.3","anchor_text":"Formula (A28) actually distributes the total energy cost and income of the who of energy they consum","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-27.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The SDR mechanism specifies the implementation model clearly. An iterative bidding and pricing process is adopted, and the contents of bid are specified in detail as described in Formula (A18). The other two mechanisms, MMR and BS, specify the contents of bid as well, as described in Formula (A24) and (A18) respectively, but do not specify if they are implemented in a one-shot or iterative way. In this paper, they are assumed to be implemented in an iterative way that is the same as that in the SDR mechanism. The reason is twofold: one is to make it convenient to compare the three mechanisms; the other is that the iterative process can also be seen as the procedure to work out the equilibrium that is used in the one-shot implementation."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.1","anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. bid of the previous iteration with Δ = rmp ·|e ibid− 1 |. Besides, if the upper di bo","equation_id":"9","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The step length control can also be achieved by limiting the number of the bids allowed to be changed at each iteration. That is,\n   e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i,j} = e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i−1,j}    j \\in \\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}} \\subset \\mathcal{PA}                                         (9)\nwhere j is the index of prosumer agent. \\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}} is the set of prosumer agents who are forbidden to change their energy bids at the i th iteration. The number of the elements in \\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}}, i.e. |\\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}}|, is pre-deﬁned. During simulation, Formula (9) should be added to the decision-making model (as described by Formula (3)) of jth prosumer agent to make it function. ... At each iteration, the elements of \\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}}, i.e. the prosumers who are forbidden to change their bids, are evenly randomly selected by the coordinator to ensure the fairness among prosumers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e24","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.1","anchor_text":"in vergence performance. The eﬀects of this measure with diﬀerent por- re tions of prosumers forbidd","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Note that the two types of step length control patterns are able to be used in a combined way to obtain smaller step limits. That is, one can ﬁrst limit the number of bids allowed to be changed as described in Formula (9), and then limit the change of the allowable bids by using Formula (8). For example, a broader ramping rate, denoted as rmp′, can be deﬁned, indicating that rmp′ × 100% of the bids are allowed to be changed and the change for each bid should not exceed ± rmp′ × 100%."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e31","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.3","anchor_text":"y g ( vergence obtained in this way may be far from the feasible optimum). ti th 3.3.3. Practical im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In practice, this can be realised by the coordinator through setting bidding rules in the implementation model, as described in Section 3.2.4, in a P2P energy sharing mechanism. For example, the mechanism can achieve this by requiring that the coordinator should reject any bid that exceeds the prescribed ramping rate so that all the prosumers have to obey the ramping rate limit. Therefore, the step length control technique in simulation is able to suggest better bidding rules in the implementation model in practice."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M02-coordination","v141-a-M03-bidding","v141-a-M03-coordination"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E04","quote":"At each iteration, the elements of 𝓟𝓐^{forbid}, i.e. the prosumers who are forbidden to change their bids, are evenly randomly selected by the coordinator to ensure the fairness among prosumers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","quote":"𝓟𝓐^{forbid} is the set of prosumer agents who are forbidden to change their energy bids at the i th iteration. The number of the elements in 𝓟𝓐^{forbid}, i.e. |𝓟𝓐^{forbid}|, is pre-defined."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E11","quote":"For example, the mechanism can achieve this by requiring that the coordinator should reject any bid that exceeds the prescribed ramping rate so that all the prosumers have to obey the ramping rate limit."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-11","quote":"An iterative bidding and pricing process is adopted, and the contents of bid are specified in detail as described in Formula (A18)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-04","quote":"Specifically, based on the results of the decision-making model presented in Section A.1, the energy bid of a prosumer is given by"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-05","quote":"\\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^- = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A} \\}  (A22)"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e22","quote":"Taking the energy bidding process in iterative implementation as an example, the step length control can be achieved by requiring each prosumer agent to limit the ramping rate of the bid at each iteration:"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E02","quote":"bid of the previous iteration with Δ = rmp ·|e_{i-1}^{bid}|. Besides, if the upper bound specified in this way exceeds the maximum limit of the energy bid e^{max}, it should be reduced to e^{max} by having min(e_{i-1}^{bid} + Δ, e^{max}). Similar operation applies to the case of the lower bound."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E03","quote":"Note that the two types of step length control patterns are able to be used in a combined way to obtain smaller step limits. That is, one can first limit the number of bids allowed to be changed as described in Formula (9), and then limit the change of the allowable bids by using Formula (8)."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"0166dfa9483856695f56cdf4277130938b0ae308b40ca1af696714adc8209272","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The core supply-bid update constraints have source-supported expressions: C001 transcribes the bid-count freeze rule from Formula (9), C004 transcribes the ramping-rate bound from Formula (8), and C005 formalizes the combined control as the conjunction of the frozen-bid subset and the ramping restriction on allowable bids. C002 remains a procedural enforcement action with no explicit formula. C003's Formula (A18) content specification depends on decision-model variables and parameters outside this rule's frozen V/E and is retained as not_formalized. B evidence in this experiment is unreviewed; no independent source audit is claimed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-x-01","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"The energy-bid variable is the supply-submission object whose update is constrained by the coordinator's bid-count and ramping rules; edge E001 represents the coordinator's limiting relation on bidding.supply."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-th-rmp","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"The ramping-rate parameter is prescribed by the coordinator and applied to supply-bid updates through the limits edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-th-emin","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"The minimum energy-bid limit clips the lower bound of the ramping constraint on the supply bid, within the coordinator's limiting relation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-th-emax","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"The maximum energy-bid limit clips the upper bound of the ramping constraint on the supply bid, within the coordinator's limiting relation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-th-forbid","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"The forbidden set is selected by the coordinator and freezes the supply bids of its members, implementing the coordinator's limiting relation on bidding.supply."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-th-forbid-size","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"The pre-defined forbidden-set size is a coordinator-side control parameter for the bid-count step-length rule."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-th-rmp-prime","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"The broader ramping rate parameterises the combined step-length control applied to the subset of allowable supply bids."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"Formula (9) formalizes the coordinator-selected forbidden set freezing supply bids, matching the limits edge from coordination.local_operator to bidding.supply."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"The procedural rejection rule is an enforcement of the coordinator's limits relation over supply submissions; it is not given a mathematical expression in the supplied source."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The SDR supply-bid content specification is attached to the bidding.supply node; full A18 formalization would require decision-model variables outside this rule's frozen graph, so no edge is asserted beyond the declared member."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C004","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"Formula (8) formalizes the ramping-rate bound on supply-bid updates, matching the coordinator's limits relation over bidding.supply."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C005","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"The combined control composes the bid-count freeze and ramping bound, both of which are coordinator limits on supply-bid updates."}],"revision_requests":["C003: If the Formula (A18) energy-bid content specification is to be fully formalized inside this rule, C.1 should confirm whether the decision-model variables x_{δ,t}, x_t^{ch}, x_t^{dis} and parameters η^{ch}, η^{dis}, P^{must-run}, P_{PV}, A_f are in scope. They are not in R002's frozen V/E, so A18 is retained as not_formalized rather than importing cross-rule mathematics.","C002: The practical enforcement action ('coordinator rejects any bid that exceeds the prescribed ramping rate') is stated procedurally and has no explicit mathematical formula in the supplied evidence. A C.1/B re-extraction would be needed to identify a formal admission/rejection predicate and its timing if that enforcement is to be represented algebraically."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
